<===> README.md
# Microsoft filter syntax in alpha() and opacity()

An empty unquoted string was checked for the filter syntax by dereferencing
the begin of the empty string (undefined behavior).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> filter/input.scss
a {b: alpha(opacity=50)}
<===> filter/output.css
a {
  b: alpha(opacity=50);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> filter_multiple/input.scss
a {b: alpha(opacity=50, foo=1)}
<===> filter_multiple/output.css
a {
  b: alpha(opacity=50, foo=1);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> filter_whitespace/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: alpha(string.unquote("opacity = 50"))}
<===> filter_whitespace/output.css
a {
  b: alpha(opacity = 50);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/alpha_empty/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: alpha(string.unquote(""))}
<===> error/alpha_empty/error
Error: $color:  is not a color.
  ,
2 | a {b: alpha(string.unquote(""))}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
<===> error/alpha_empty/error-libsass
Error: $color:  is not a color.
  ,
2 | a {b: alpha(string.unquote(""))}
  |                            ^^
  '
  input.scss 2:28  alpha()
  ,
2 | a {b: alpha(string.unquote(""))}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7   root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/multiple_empty/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: alpha(opacity=50, string.unquote(""))}
